# okf-template-sync manifest (D-12): the contract of which files this template OWNS.
#
# `okf-template-sync` overwrites exactly the files listed here, from a later template tag, in one reviewable pull
# request; a file listed in this repository's previous manifest and dropped from a later one is DELETED in that pull
# request. Removing a line is therefore not a cleanup: it deletes the file in every repository on its next sync.
#
# One repository-relative path per line (letters, digits, dot, underscore, dash and slash; no leading dash, no dot or
# dot-dot component); `#` starts a comment line. The single special line below, `merge-codeowners`, merges CODEOWNERS:
# every existing line is kept and a template rule the repository lacks is appended with the owners of its own
# `/.github/` rule.
#
# KB-owned files are NEVER listed and the sync refuses a manifest that names one (the deny-list is in template-sync.sh,
# not here): the knowledge bundle, `.okf/maintainers`, `.okf/publish.toml`, `.okf/profile.json`, `.okf/agent.toml`,
# `.okf/template-version`, `README.md`, the CODEOWNERS owner lines, and the rules skill's run-time profile render.
